# Jira Sub-task

**Use for:** a thin child slice under an existing parent issue (implementation
step, investigation spike, follow-up fix).

**Create only** when the user explicitly names sub-task / subtask. Default
creates are Story, Bug, or Task (`jira-create`).

## Create

1. Parent must already exist (or be created in the same authorized turn).
2. Set the parent link on create — never orphan a sub-task.
3. Summary names the slice, not the whole parent outcome.

## Description

Keep short:

```markdown
## Overview

<What this child slice delivers relative to the parent.>
```

Add numbered Requirements / AC only when the slice has its own measurable
checks beyond the parent. Prefer inheriting parent AC when the slice is purely
mechanical.

## Done

Done when the child slice’s Overview (and AC when present) is complete. Parent
status is separate — finishing a sub-task does not auto-close the parent.
Status moves: `jira-status`.
